{
  "dom_id": "step-q6086",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Which three numbers **CANNOT** be the measures of the sides of a triangle?",
  "worked_solution": "The triangle inequality theorem states that the length of any one side must be smaller than the sum of the other two sides.\n\nIn particular, for the numbers $17,9,8$ to represent the sides of a triangle, the number $17$ must be smaller than the sum of the numbers $9$ and $8.$ But this is not the case:\n\n$$\n9+8=17≯17\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three numbers $17,9,8$ cannot represent the sides of a triangle.",
